sp("V04-D-010", "Science and environment", "Bleached corals are often alive and can recover, so what matters is the time a reef gets between hot spells.", "Easy",
   ["A reef that has bleached looks, from a boat, like a field of white bones, and it is natural to assume that the corals beneath have died.",
    "Often they have not, at least not yet.",
    "Bleaching happens when prolonged heat leads a coral to eject the single-celled algae that live in its tissues and feed it, and the pale colour is simply the skeleton seen through tissue that has lost its tenants.",
    "The animal itself is still alive, though it is now going hungry, because those algae supplied most of its food.",
    "If the water cools within a few weeks, many corals take in fresh algae from the surrounding sea and gradually regain their colour and their strength.",
    "A reef that has lost many of its corals, however, may take many years to rebuild, as new colonies settle and grow."],
   "What matters most, then, is not whether a single hot spell strikes but how long the reef is given to recover before the next one.",
   [0, 2, 3, 6],
   "The missing sentence is a conclusion ('then') about the time a reef needs to recover. It depends on the last two sentences, which describe how quickly individual corals can recover and how slowly a badly damaged reef rebuilds. So it closes the paragraph at gap (4).",
   {0: "At gap (1) nothing has been said about hot spells or recovery, so there is nothing for 'then' to conclude from.",
    2: "At gap (2) the sentence would cut 'Often they have not' off from the explanation of what bleaching is, and no recovery has yet been described.",
    3: "At gap (3) the sentence would split the explanation of bleaching from 'The animal itself is still alive', which completes it, and the recovery that the conclusion relies on is still to come."},
   "Placing the sentence at gap (3), as if the mention of heat in the bleaching sentence were enough to support the conclusion.",
   "V04D-coral-bleaching-symbiosis", "A conclusion marker that depends on the two recovery sentences fixes the last gap; the other gaps fall before recovery is mentioned.",
   cognitive="Understanding")

