sp("V04-D-011", "Science and environment", "No-till farming protects soil, but its value for storing carbon is less certain than once hoped.", "Medium",
   ["Ploughing turns the soil over, buries weeds and leaves a clean bed for seed, which is why it has been the default on so many farms.",
    "It also exposes buried organic matter to air, so that microbes break it down faster and release its carbon as carbon dioxide.",
    "Farming without ploughing, in which seed is drilled directly into the stubble of the last crop, has therefore been promoted as a way of keeping carbon in the ground.",
    "Measurements have complicated that hope.",
    "Untilled fields often hold more carbon near the surface, but some of that gain appears to be offset by less carbon deeper down, where the plough used to carry crop residues.",
    "None of this makes the method worthless, since unploughed soil is far less prone to washing and blowing away.",
    "It does mean that its value is better argued on the ground of protecting soil than on the ground of storing carbon."],
   "Some advocates have gone further and presented it as a major answer to climate change, on the grounds that farmland covers so much of the earth.",
   [1, 2, 3, 5],
   "The missing sentence has 'gone further' than the claim that farming without ploughing keeps carbon in the ground, and its 'it' must be that method. It then sets up the hope that 'Measurements have complicated'. So it sits between the promotion of the method and the measurements, at gap (3).",
   {1: "At gap (1) the only practice mentioned is ploughing, so 'it' would make ploughing the answer to climate change, the reverse of the paragraph's point, and there is no earlier claim for 'gone further' to go beyond.",
    2: "At gap (2) farming without ploughing has still not been introduced; 'it' would again mean ploughing, which has just been blamed for releasing carbon.",
    5: "At gap (4) the measurements have already undercut the carbon claim, so a sentence enlarging that claim would come too late, and it would separate 'None of this' from the measurements it refers to."},
   "Placing the sentence at gap (4), reading it as a further point after the measurements rather than as an inflated hope that the measurements answer.",
   "V04D-soil-tillage-carbon", "The solver must resolve 'it' to the right farming method and see that the inflated claim must precede the evidence that tempers it.")

